Java 4 Days Bootcamp – Project Submission

📌 Project Problem Statement

Develop Java programs to demonstrate fundamental Java programming concepts, including user input, conditional statements, loops, classes, objects, constructors, methods, inheritance, abstraction, and runtime polymorphism.

The project aims to strengthen programming skills through practical problem-solving exercises and object-oriented programming.

📌 Project Description

This project is a collection of Java programs developed as part of the Java 4 Days Bootcamp.

It demonstrates basic Java programming techniques and Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts through practical examples.

The programs cover personal information display, age eligibility checking, star pattern printing, bank account management, animal inheritance, and shape area calculation using abstraction and polymorphism.

✨ Key Features

1. Personal Information: Displays personal details using Java output statements.
2. Age Eligibility Checker: Accepts the user's age and checks event registration eligibility.
3. Star Pattern Printing: Uses nested loops to print a triangular star pattern.
4. Bank Account Management: Implements deposit, withdrawal, and balance display operations.
5. Animal Inheritance: Demonstrates inheritance using Animal, Dog, and Cat classes.
6. Shape Area Calculator: Calculates the areas of Circle, Rectangle, and Triangle using abstraction and polymorphism.

